WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:06.230
They back Donald Trump and want him to build
the border wall.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.649
They don't.

00:00:07.649 --> 00:00:13.240
Opponents and supporters of the US president
facing each other in McAllen while waiting

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.240
for his arrival.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.900
I was born and raised in the valley and I
feel it is very important that we secure our

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:18.900
borders.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.110
It is absolutely important, it is necessary
for my children, for my safety.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:26.230
The wall is just a scapegoat for all the problems
that the US has.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.860
People think that because the border wall
is going be build up, all the world's problems

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.000
are going to be fixed.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.360
Our country's problems are going to be fixed.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.690
But it's not true.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:37.920
Members of the same community, but deeply
divided.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.260
A couple lost their temper, the police had
to intervene.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:47.210
Meanwhile, President Trump was given a tour
along the Rio Grande, where he talked to border

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:53.890
agents, using this trip to bolster his argument
for his signature campaign promise.

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:58.649
What they need more than anything is the barrier
or the wall, call it whatever you want whether

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:02.520
it is steel or concrete you don't care, we
need a barrier.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:07.310
In McAllen, Trump once again threatened to
invoke emergency powers to build the wall

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:09.690
without Congressional approval.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:12.700
But many in the Rio Grande valley disagree.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:16.130
They don't see a reason to declare a national
emergency here.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:20.470
Most people we talked to at the protest told
us they feel safe that there is no crisis

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:24.830
at the border, they accuse the president of
stoking fear in their community.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.740
Even some of Trump supporters told us that
they do want tighter security, but that they

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:35.909
don't think that a border is going to solve
all problems.

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:39.400
Brandy Kennedy has lived in McAllen for twelve
years.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.930
She says she is proud of her community.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:45.310
This is the safest place I've ever lived in
my life.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:52.350
So the whole idea that there is hoodlums coming
over illegally, and drugs in the streets and

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.350
cartels is ridiculous.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:56.520
It is absolutely not.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:02.060
She says if President Trump stayed long enough
in McAllen to see that for himself, maybe

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.109
he'd change his mind.

